{
  "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
  "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "William E. Marsh (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Armed Career Criminal Act enhances the punishment for possession of a firearm or ammunition for a person who has three previous convictions for a violent felony. This case involves, as you know, vehicular fleeing, which Indiana has divided into five categories. Indiana statute treats vehicular fleeing as a continuum of behavior ranging from merely failing to stop, on the low end, which is the crime Mr. Sykes was convicted of violating, all the way to fleeing which results in the death of a police officer, on the high end, which in Indiana is a class A felony."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What's in between?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: You're supposed to stop dead in your tracks and not pull off on the shoulder?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "William E. Marsh (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The prosecutor is not under any obligation; was that the question, Justice Alito?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: My problem is there is arguably not here a gradation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I wouldn't say that they didn't have a rational basis for dividing it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Since 1998, I have found 14 cases in the Indiana Court of Appeals, one of which is the Hape case that Justice Alito cited earlier. All of them, so far as I can tell, proceeded under (A) and not under (B)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's four times as risky as arson in terms of injuries and fatalities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could I ask you this: If a person is convicted of vehicular flight that causes death, is that aggressive conduct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WALL: Yes, the Government would say it is, Justice Alito."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Doesn't whether it's aggressive or not depend upon how it happened? I mean, it could be -- I mean, the flight puts in place the potential for -- for violence, I agree with that; but if somebody just, you know, jumps out between two cars while the fellow's fleeing, how has his conduct changed to aggressive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But he's saying even when it's risky, it's not aggressive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WALL: Yes, on a case-by-case basis. But, categorically, which is what this Court looks at, the conduct encompassed by the elements in the ordinary case -- in the ordinary case -- the character of the conduct is aggressive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Suppose you have one of 36 States which treat this -- treat the general offense as a misdemeanor and then make it a felony if you put somebody at risk. Just reading that statute, you'd think those 36 States, when they have the general offense, do something where the guy acted pretty trivially; and where it's a felony, he actually put somebody at risk, sped off -- wouldn't that be your normal instinct in just guessing from the -- from the language?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WALL: The States treat it differently."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: You can't commit (B) without committing (A) first. (B) has just one additional element, but all of the elements of (A) are part of the elements of (B). So, how can it not be a lesser included?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ecaa56a7caa977ec65bfe63a645f857a3c4ba162cc4132ec5516e2dd96668875",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ecaa56a7caa9-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WALL: Your Honor, the Government does not think that (A) is a lesser included of (B)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-11311",
      "confidence": 0.0,
